<h4 id="about-variable-scope">About variable scope</h4>

<p>The kinds of parameter variables that may be used in a C function:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Parameter types</li>
  <li>Automatic variables (local variables)</li>
  <li>Static variables (static local variables)</li>
  <li>Static global variables</li>
  <li>Global variables</li>
</ul>

<p>Because of their special storage regions, three of these variables can be called at any time and in any state:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Static variables</li>
  <li>Static global variables</li>
  <li>Global variables</li>
</ul>

<p>The other two each have their own scope; once the scope is exceeded, they get destroyed.</p>

